8\\t\\n19\\twe don't want that, we just want 1 single box that says:\\n20\\t\\n21\\t`tools called` or something similar. This box can be expanded, then we get the individual tools that were called. each individual tool can also be expanded to see the details.\\n22\\t\\n23\\t## Current state\\n24\\t\\n25\\t`buildActionConversationRenderGroups` groups each visible run of at least two adjacent completed tool calls. A run is a sequence of completed tool-call events uninterrupted by a visible message or non-completed event; completed reasoning is hidden before grouping and therefore does not split the run. Single completed calls and all running, failed, or declined calls remain standalone.\\n26\\t\\n27\\t`CompletedToolCallGroup` renders one outer border, but immediately renders every call through `ActionConversationEventRow`. Dividers make those rows touch, so the result still looks like several tool-call boxes instead of one summary box. Each row independently expands through `AgentToolEvent` or `CommandExecutionEvent` to show its details.\\n28\\t\\n29\\t## implementation details\\n30\\t\\n31\\t- Keep canonical conversation entries and `buildActionConversationRenderGroups` grouping rules unchanged. This feature changes presentation only.\\n32\\t- Render each multi-call group as one collapsed summary box labelled `Tools called (N)`, where `N` is number of calls in that group.\\n33\\t- Make summary header a button with visible expand/collapse affordance and accurate `aria-expanded` state.\\n34\\t- When summary expands, render calls in canonical conversation order as compact rows inside same outer box. Separate rows with divider hairlines; do not give each row its own outer box.\\n35\\t- Keep each call row independently expandable. Expanding one call reveals existing command or generic-tool details without collapsing group or changing expansion state of other calls.\\n36\\t- Preserve group and row keys based on existing event identities. When a running call completes and extends an existing multi-call group, mounted rows retain their expansion state and no call is duplicated.\\n37\\t- Keep single completed calls standalone. Keep running, started, in-progress, failed, and declined calls outside completed multi-call groups with existing lifecycle status and detail behavior.\\n38\\t- Use theme spacing, colors, borders, typography, and outlined MUI icons. Long summary or call text must truncate or wrap without horizontal chat overflow.\\n39\\t- Update chat rendering tests for collapsed summary, group expansion, nested independent detail expansion, grouping boundaries, live completion, accessible state, and unchanged standalone calls.\\n40\\t\\n41\\t## acceptance criteria\\n42\\t\\n43\\t- Every run containing at least two completed tool calls initially appears as one collapsed `Tools called (N)` box.\\n44\\t- Expanding summary shows every grouped call once, in original conversation order, inside same outer box.\\n45\\t- Each visible call can independently expand and collapse its existing details while summary remains expanded.\\n46\\t- Messages and visible non-completed events split groups; hidden completed reasoning does not split them.\\n47\\t- Single completed calls and non-completed calls remain standalone with existing status and detail behavior.\\n48\\t- A call that completes during live rendering can extend an existing adjacent multi-call group without duplication or loss of existing row expansion state.\\n49\\t- Summary and call controls expose accessible names and correct `aria-expanded` values.\\n50\\t- Group contents do not cause horizontal overflow in conversation chat.\\n51\\t\",\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json:189:          \"type\": \"reasoning\"\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json:279:          \"type\": \"reasoning\"\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json:369:          \"type\": \"reasoning\"\ndesign\\release