onfigService.config` is private; callers use `get`, `set`, and `clear`. | Module evaluation order is not guaranteed, so `configService` is not usable at import time. Reading config in a constructor is a bug. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Events and React integration\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Decision | Rule | Rationale |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| Services notify observers through their own `EventTarget`. | Services expose an `EventTarget` and dispatch named `CustomEvent` domain events such as `activeIndex`, `added`, `deleted`, or `changedBox`. Observers subscribe with `addEventListener` and unsubscribe with `removeEventListener` on the owning service. | Decouples producers from consumers without depending on Node `EventEmitter`, which is not available in the browser-first React app. |\\\\\\\\n| Custom hooks bridge service events to functional components. | Hooks in `src/components/hooks/`, such as `useActiveIndex` and `useProjectConfig`, seed `useState` from a service property, subscribe in `useEffect`, unsubscribe in cleanup, and return the value. Prefer hook + service over prop chains. | Components stay declarative and avoid direct event plumbing. |\\\\\\\\n| Components subscribe at the smallest rendering boundary. | Root and layout components compose UI regions and pass structural inputs. Components that render changing application data subscribe through hooks themselves. Do not hoist changing data into ancestors only to pass it downward. | Limits rerenders to affected UI, protects transient state such as open popups, and avoids broad prop chains. |\\\\\\\\n| Components use the app theme service path. | `App` owns theme mode through `useThemeMode()`, builds the MUI theme with `createAppTheme(mode)`, and provides it through `ThemeProvider`. Components read theme values with MUI APIs such as `useTheme`, `useMediaQuery`, and `sx`; only controls that change the palette mode receive `mode` and `onToggleTheme`. | Theme state, persistence, and palette construction stay centralized while components remain presentation-focused. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"workingDirectory\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\janbo\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Documents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\md2_workers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dev1\\\\\\\"\\\\n        },\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"agent-turn-75713909-e67d-45bc-a4d1-233f192f2a33-event-8\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Reasoning\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"providerItemId\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rs_0310a9445750e6ae016a71ced47cc48191b18c744c42b5e1bd\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"sequence\\\\\\\": 8,\\\\n          \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-08-04T11:36:52.540Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"reasoning\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n          \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": []\\\\n        },\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"agent\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Spec confirms two required changes, one optional optimization, profiler acceptance. Inspecting components, selectors, registry identity behavior, existing tests before block plan.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"agent-turn-75713909-e67d-45bc-a4d1-233f192f2a33-turn-1-assistant-2\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"sequence\\\\\\\": 9,\\\\n          \\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-08-04T11:36:53.812Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n        },\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"app/src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\actions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\action_run_registry.ts:152:function eventIdentity(event: AgentConversa