0:internalId: fe82e636-7ea7-4703-acb8-086b0001c3b8\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_057_edit_prepared_action_prompt.md:22:internalId: 3b658638-4f2e-43d3-9435-16bc50225ae0\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_059_mobile_toolbar.md:10:internalId: d70fa2aa-557e-4664-951e-c68e389ee194\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_001_initialize.md:10:internalId: 7cdce4fa-014d-4364-ba6c-a3446da07136\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_056_root_action_commit_history.md:17:internalId: 8ede12bb-dc50-4adc-a9ef-7ae48e6f3f05\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_056_root_action_commit_history.md:79:- Card rename/move keeps activity ownership because storage is keyed by stable `header.internalId`; historical body lookup still uses the card's current path, so rename tracking is outside this feature.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_058_compact_action_usage_summary.md:17:internalId: 3b72e774-8764-4e0a-a4b9-5dcad3797add\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_055_agent_file_change_tracking.md:10:internalId: def715be-87f5-4226-9f9e-0d1bb9ef058a\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_015_split_github_storage_service.md:10:internalId: a286893a-19e5-47bb-a427-d562b5fd5eb5\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_005_split_data_service_collaborators.md:10:internalId: 08c2a65f-83b0-4d55-8f82-e8990db2fe32\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_008_split_action_runner_helpers.md:10:internalId: e21ca7ec-787c-4d43-9bde-6e8d657bedb8\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_003_refactor_cleanup_dead_files_and_shims.md:10:internalId: 435f2810-f697-41bf-8df2-1c82a7eec6d4\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_009_split_config_service.md:10:internalId: 108da9da-165a-47db-8b7b-5c77a5b25f79\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_013_action_runner_dependency_surface.md:10:internalId: dcf55c60-4777-4137-bd32-8a59ac175af9\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_011_narrow_data_service_context.md:10:internalId: d53a66b3-a644-4cea-a362-dd1a4accca62\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_010_split_action_popup.md:10:internalId: a292676b-17a9-4868-b17c-52be9c505bcc\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_054_agent_token_usage_tracking.md:10:internalId: c91d54de-c049-4b03-b689-b26a19e9086b\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_007_split_action_scheduler_service.md:10:internalId: bf0bfb85-fc1f-441d-8e1d-7e90d09e568d\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_014_split_data_service_tests.md:10:internalId: 44f871b5-dca7-4907-afa6-07137190c002\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:32:internalId: 0e5b7d15-ad4d-4c58-b15b-8d03dcd7caac\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:51:- `ActionContext` has the card path but not its stable `header.internalId`;\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:65:One card file owns all action-run and conversation activity for that card, filed by `header.internalId` — never path, title, display id, or normalized path prefix.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:105:- `SourceCommit` icon in the card popup header, between Dirty/Saved and Close; same control in `ListEditorToolbarControls` beside Agents/Properties for file-mode cards.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_006_split_local_git_service.md:10:internalId: d86531c8-0d02-4714-b860-aaaf1ed856a3\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_004_split_project_toolbar_menu_dialogs.md:10:internalId: 4853842f-cb89-4633-a5cb-539574addeeb\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_019_unify_open_document_drafts_and_save_state.md:28:internalId: 620ef9b2-2365-4963-aee1-0dd5c894b4f7\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_019_unify_open_document_drafts_and_save_state.md:72:The active target pairs the canonical action document with its section. Section identity routes outgoing text, external replacement, undo history, and phrase deletion. It never owns dirty state and is not encoded as a public namespaced `markdownDocumentId`. Card body uses one implicit `body` section.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_012_unify_react_electron_validators.md:10:internalId: c606cf96-16bf-4d0b-b936-d7fc406a3514\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\J_26_add_new_card_is_slow.md:4:internalId: 49897820-6770-45cf-80e6-250f2bb2a4ca\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_018_extract_project_persistence_coordinator.md:28:internalId: 4a1ef679-b831-463e-ac6c-537207708319\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:34:internalId: ade374a9-a511-4a2c-88b5-710c51f5447b\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:39:Replace props derived from global snapshots with stable Markdown data sources: they resolve current domain objects, notify editors of document-specific changes, and accept document-aware writes. Each editing binding owns its own editor and undo store.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:41:Result: save-state transitions and unrelated card/action changes no longer replace editor content or re-render editor owners. Document content, commit batching, dirty tracking, undo semantics, and persisted data stay unchanged unless noted here.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:57:**Renewable domain objects** — `ProjectState` reuses a `ProjectCard` object while content/sha/activity/conversations are unchanged, and only creates a new object on genuine renewal. Cards have stable `header.internalId`; paths are persistence addresses, not identity. `ActionService` produces renewable `ActionDefinition`s, but some action-editor-state changes mutate the existing object and still emit `changed` — object identity alone isn't a complete action-tab signal.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:67:- **Markdown document ID**: stable identity of one editable Markdown body. Card body ID = `card.header.internalId`. Action prompt/phrase IDs combine namespace, action ID, and stable editor document ID.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:151:`CardMarkdownDataSource` resolves card bodies by `header.internalId` through current `DataService` snapshot objects.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:159:Card paths never form a Markdown document ID: rename preserves identity/history because `internalId` is unchanged. Missing `internalId` fails fast.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:187:When renewed content equals the last written content: the originating binding ignores the echo (cursor/undo stay intact); another binding currently showing the same document is replaced and re-baselined (so board and list can't diverge); unrelated bindings receive nothing. Needed because board and list may independently bind the same card while both stay mounted.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:315:- Card Markdown document ID is `header.internalId`; file rename preserves identity and history.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:317:- Echo tracking is per Markdown document, preserving originating cursor/undo while syncing another bound editor.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:12:internalId: 75426a89-612e-481c-9fd5-eb269a3b8c98\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:210:Make cancellation and root-phase failure metadata explicit rather than continuing to attach undocumented properties throughout the facade. Because the style guide requires every class in its own file, place any new error class in its own module. Do not introduce a hierarchy unless both cancellation and phase propagation need distinct behavior.\n",
