\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:371:        configService.init()\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_control_connection.test.ts:3:    configureRemoteControlConnection,\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_control_connection.test.ts:26:        configureRemoteControlConnection({ endpoint: 'ws://127.0.0.1:1234', token: 'token-1' })\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:14:Support batch/PowerShell/bash scripts (with parameters and placeholders) in configurable folders as runnable actions; the Electron app monitors these folders and adds/updates/removes the related actions, notifying the React app of changes. Extension to `design\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_010_actions.md`\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:17:Not implemented. F-010 action loading/running is also not implemented yet. The Electron app currently exposes only local Git/data bridge methods, watches markdown changes under the project root and has no script-folder config, script discovery, command runner, parameter model or action-change notification channel.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:20:- Extend the F-010 action model with generated `command` actions sourced from configured script folders. Every generated action has a stable `id` that does not depend on its editable name.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:24:- Execute scripts through the Electron action runner with explicit interpreters: Windows command processor for `.bat`/`.cmd`, Windows PowerShell 5.x for `.ps1` and a configured bash executable for `.sh`.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:25:- Watch configured folders, debounce reloads and publish action-list updates to React when scripts or sidecar json files are added, changed or removed.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:26:- Fail fast with clear load/run errors for invalid sidecar json, duplicate generated action names, unsupported extensions, missing configured folders, missing bash executable or attempts to run outside the configured folders.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:30:- Opening a local Electron project loads script actions from configured project and Electron script folders.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:32:- Running `.bat`, `.cmd`, `.ps1` and configured `.sh` scripts executes through Electron with placeholders and configured parameters resolved.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_connect_string.ts:6: * desktop `buildConnectUrl`; parsing lets the web connect dialog fill endpoint + token in one paste.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_010_actions.md:41:- For agent actions, show extra prompt input and the supported per-run agent/model/thinking-level choices. Model choices come from configured profiles with built-in defaults; thinking choices are `none`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, and `max`.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_010_actions.md:43:- Execute `onBefore` -> main -> matching `on` actions -> `onAfter` in configured order. Reject cycles before execution.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:17:New cards are created through `DataService.createCard` and `createCardFile`. File naming uses the configured card type prefix and next available number, and generated markdown now goes through `markdownParsingService.buildCardMarkdown`. The generated header includes `id`, `internalId`, `title`, `status: new` and `affects`, followed by a title heading and the body entered in the new-card form. There is no configured body template yet, and new-card generation still does not write `author`, `owner` or `policy`.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:26:- Keep id generation and file naming in `card_naming.ts`: use the configured card type prefix and next available number across working folder and subfolders.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:30:- Creating a new card writes a markdown file named `{id}-{title}.md` in the configured working folder.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:31:- The new file contains the configured body template and a frontmatter header with `author`, `id`, `internalId`, `title`, `status`, `owner`, `affects` and `policy`.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\test_support\\\\\\\\data_service_test_support.ts:119:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => ({ backgroundShade: 'blue' as const, projectFolder: '', workingFolder: 'design' })),\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\test_support\\\\\\\\data_service_test_support.ts:122:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:14:Provide a custom dialog to easily edit the `affects` list of a card, with a dropdown of proposed repo files filtered on what is already typed.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:17:Still not implemented (confirmed by the 2026-07 implementation audit). `CardHeader.affects` exists as `string[]`, is parsed by `markdownParsingService` from `affects:` frontmatter lists and is searchable through F-017, and `markdownParsingService.rewriteListLines` already rewrites list fields generically (used for `agents:` references via `setAgentLogReferences`) — but there is no public affects-specific rewrite helper on `DataService`. The card UI (card view, body dialog, text view) has no `affects` editing surface. The storage contract (`StorageService` in `app/src/data/data_types.ts`) still has no repository file listing, so no suggestion source exists for either GitHub or local projects.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:23:- Add an affects editor dialog reachable from the card/editor UI. It shows current affected files, supports add/remove, and uses a typed file picker filtered by the current input.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:34:- Tests cover parsing-service header rewrite behavior, duplicate/self-path exclusion, filtered suggestions, and save flow from the dialog.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_019_telemetry.md:19:- Keep DSNs/app keys in untracked local config files or environment variables per subproject; tracked sample files may document required names but must not contain real keys.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_019_telemetry.md:29:- React and Electron initialize Sentry and Aptabase when local keys are configured, and run without telemetry failures when keys are missing.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:4:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:48:const configuredProfileProvider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:59:        const profile = findAgentProfile(configService.get('desktop.agentProfiles'), agent)\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:79:    constructor(provider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = configuredProfileProvider) {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_types.ts:5:export const PROJECT_CONFIG_PATH = 'md2.config.json'\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:14:Provide a global theme service (light/dark, flat look, configurable color scheme with preview, configurable markdown styles with pre-built defaults) that all components refresh from, including reading the theme in Electron before the main window is created.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:17:Theming is minimal ([[F-004]]): `createAppTheme(mode)` in `theme/appTheme.ts` just returns `createTheme({ palette: { mode } })`, and `useThemeMode` (`theme/useThemeMode.ts`) tracks light/dark, persisting the choice to `localStorage` (`md2.themeMode`) with an OS-preference fallback. `App` builds the theme and provides it via MUI `ThemeProvider`; `mode`/`onToggleTheme` are threaded as props through `MainWindow` and `MainToolbar` rather than read from a service. There is no configurable color scheme, no flat/round/borderless styling, no markdown style config, and `CardTypeConfig` (`data/dataTypes.ts`) has no color. On the desktop, `desktop/main.js` creates the `BrowserWindow` with default chrome and never reads the theme, so the window buttons are unstyled.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:22:- Configurable color scheme: expose editable `primary`/`secondary`/… roles each with `light`/`regular`/`dark` variants, feed them into the palette, and offer a live preview while editing.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:23:- Configurable markdown styles: define a style config mapping each markdown section (title1, title2, caption, body, …) to font/color/size/formatting; ship pre-built defaults (`modern`, `classic`, `serif`, `sans-serif`, `handwritten`) selectable by the user.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:31:- The color scheme (primary/secondary/… with light/regular/dark variants) is user-configurable with a live preview, and the choice persists across restarts.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:32:- Markdown section styling is configurable, with the listed pre-built defaults selectable; the selection persists across restarts.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:33:        configService.clear()\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:61:    it('loads configured profile overrides and fixed thinking levels without provider credentials', async () => {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:62:        configService.init({\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:63:            desktopConfig: {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:100:        configService.init()\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:17:`@mdxeditor/editor` is installed but still not used by any component in `app/src`; every editing surface is an interim multiline MUI `TextField`. Card view ([[F-005]]) and text view ([[F-006]]) are both implemented and wired through `ProjectWorkspace`, so `ProjectWorkspace` no longer edits a card directly — it delegates to `CardView` and `TextView` and forwards their changes to `DataService`. Card body editing goes through `CardBodyEditor` (used by the desktop `CardBodyDialog` and mobile accordion), whose `onBodyChange` calls `DataService.updateCardBody`; that method already uses the shared `markdownParsingService.replaceBody` to preserve the frontmatter/header block and replace only the body. Text view edits full file content in a per-tab `TextField` and saves via the same `onBodyChange`/`DataService` path. Both `CardBodyEditor` and the text-view editor carry TODO notes that the MDXEditor component and its formatting toolbar land with F-007 and replace them. There is still no shared editor component and no formatting toolbar (sticky or otherwise).\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:23:- Replace the current `ProjectWorkspace` textarea path with the shared editor, then reuse the same component in card dialog/mobile accordion and future file tabs.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_017_search.md:21:The top shell is `MainToolbar` (MUI `AppBar`/`Toolbar`) rendered by `MainWindow`; it holds the \\\\\\\"MD²\\\\\\\" title, a config `IconButton` and a `toolbarAction` slot (currently `<ThemeControls />` from `app.tsx`). There is no search input in the toolbar. The desktop window is borderless via Electron `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'` with a `titleBarOverlay` in `desktop/main.js`; there is no manual CSS drag region (`-webkit-app-region`) anywhere in the React shell, so a custom drag bar and its non-draggable input/button zones do not yet exist.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_017_search.md:23:Navigation into a card/file is local to `ProjectWorkspace`, which owns `viewMode` (`'cards' | 'text'`). `handleOpenInFileMode(path)` sets a `requestedPath` + `requestedNonce` and switches to text view; `TextView` opens that path as a tab via `useOpenTabs` and can browse background files through its file tree. There is no shared/global \\\\\\\"navigate to card or file, keeping current view\\\\\\\" API — selecting a background result without changing view mode is not currently supported. Routing exists via `app_navigation` (`navigateTo` / `useAppLocation`, with a `/config` route), but nothing search-related uses it.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:6:    ProjectConfig,\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:10:import { GithubProjectConfigStorage } from './github_project_config_storage'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:23:    private readonly configStorage: GithubProjectConfigStorage\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:33:        this.configStorage = new GithubProjectConfigStorage(this.context, gitData, this.writer)\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:64:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference) {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:65:        return this.configStorage.loadProjectConfig(project)\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:104:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig) {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:105:        return this.configStorage.saveProjectConfig(project, config)\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:3:title: config\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:13:> **NOTE 2026-07-11:** The `window.md2GithubAuth` bridge and GitHub OAuth proxy referenced below were removed with OAuth (see [[F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy]]). GitHub auth is now PAT-only and the `connection` config section no longer exists.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:16:Provide a browsable `/config` page with sections and quick-jump tabs, typed value editors with descriptions, explicit save/cancel, and a global config service that merges values from React-app, desktop-app and project-level sources depending on the connection setup.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:19:Config is still handled by separate feature-specific paths. There is no `/config` route, no router-backed navigation, no config page UI, no draft save/cancel flow and no singleton `ConfigService`. The shared `service_injector` exists and `DataService` registers itself there, but config is passed directly into `DataService.init`.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:21:Project config is a small in-memory object. `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` builds it from hard-coded/default values: working folder `design`, default card types, default card body template and the selected push mode. `ProjectWorkspace` owns the push-mode select, recreates config when opening a GitHub or local project, and reads card types/working folder back from `DataService`. `use_app_bootstrap.ts` restores the last project with auto push mode. No project config file is loaded, merged, validated or saved.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:23:GitHub auth config is read from Vite environment values by `readGithubAuthConfig`; missing `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` fails fast, optional proxy URL can be absent and scopes default to `repo`. Theme settings are persisted separately in `localStorage` through `useThemeSettings`, not through a general config system.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:25:Electron exposes local data, GitHub OAuth proxy and theme-mode bridges on `window.md2Data`, `window.md2GithubAuth` and `window.md2Theme`. The desktop app URL is resolved from `MD2_APP_URL` with a localhost default. There is no desktop config bridge for editable settings and no project-level config IPC/storage contract.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:27:Tests cover the current focused paths: project/session data behavior, GitHub auth config, theme settings/provider, Electron app URL resolution and desktop theme helpers. There are no config-service merge/validation tests or config-page React tests yet.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:30:- Add a singleton `ConfigService` in `app/src/services/`, registered through `service_injector`, with two-phase initialization and explicit `get`, `set`, `clear`, `loadDraft`, `saveDraft` and `discardDraft` behavior.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:31:- Define config metadata separately from values: key, section, label, description, value type, allowed options/range, default value, source (`react`, `desktop`, `project`) and editability.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:32:- Replace `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` and direct config constants with values from `ConfigService`; affected call sites are `use_app_bootstrap.ts`, `project_workspace.tsx` and `data_service.ts`. They should receive the new config behavior.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:33:- Keep GitHub env config (`github_auth_config.ts`) fail-fast for required build/runtime values, but expose editable connection settings only for values that can be changed safely at runtime.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:34:- In desktop mode, expose desktop config values through the preload bridge. Use main-process IPC only for values that require main-owned Electron APIs.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:35:- Project config is loaded after a project opens, merged over defaults, and saved through the active storage backend. Missing required project config fields fail with clear errors.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:36:- Build `/config` as a real navigable route or URL-backed view. Sections use hash anchors for quick jumps; desktop shows section tabs on the left, mobile shows them below the toolbar.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:37:- The config page edits a draft only. Save validates and applies changes to services; Cancel or leaving the page clears the draft without changing active config.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:40:- `/config` can be opened directly and navigated with browser back/forward, including section hash jumps.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:41:- Config entries are grouped by section and rendered with typed editors: switch for booleans, dropdown for known values, number input or slider for numeric ranges, and short descriptions for all entries.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:42:- Save applies validated changes to the global config service and affected services; Cancel leaves the active config unchanged.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:44:- Opening a project loads project config, merges it over defaults, and uses it for working folder, push mode and card type settings.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:45:- Invalid or missing required config shows a clear error and does not silently fall back to partial behavior.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:46:- Config draft state is created only while `/config` is open and cleared when the page closes.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:47:- Unit tests cover config merge/validation and service updates; React tests cover typed editors, save/cancel and desktop/mobile section navigation.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:50:- `design\\\\\\\\architecture\\\\\\\\initial description\\\\\\\\config.md`\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:18:- Add preload bridge methods to configure/test SSH connection details, list image files on the device with modified times, import selected files and persist per-device import metadata in the project.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:29:- In Electron local-project mode, the user can configure/test a Remarkable SSH connection and list available image files with modified times.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:29:    ProjectConfig,\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:219:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null> {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:220:        return this.request<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null>('loadProjectConfig', [project])\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:296:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig